**One decision beyond the plan:** my first draft of the "keys are independent" test recorded both keys at the same t=0, so at t=windowMs both freed and the test was vacuous. I rewrote it so b fills up at t=500; at t=1000 a's events drop out while b's still block — that actually exercises per-key pruning. The failure this caused was in the test only, not the implementation. Worked on `work/main`, committed, working tree clean, no other files touched; results sent to architect.
